WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.987
Unit sixteen. Intro to Open Source!

2
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:09.625
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.544
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.594 --> 00:00:17.764
Today we learn about Intro to Open Source. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.945 --> 00:00:23.577
Open source. Say it with me. Open source!

6
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:31.294
Free to use. Say it with me. Free to use!

7
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:39.642
Community-driven. Say it with me. Community-driven!

8
00:00:43.111 --> 00:00:47.744
Collaborate publicly. Say it with me. Collaborate publicly!

9
00:00:51.285 --> 00:00:55.018
License. Say it with me. License!

10
00:00:58.528 --> 00:01:02.846
Shared code. Say it with me. Shared code!

11
00:01:06.296 --> 00:01:09.863
Contribute. Say it with me. Contribute!

12
00:01:13.425 --> 00:01:18.275
Public repository. Say it with me. Public repository!

13
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:31.892
Open source software is free to use, with shared code in a public repository. A community collaborates publicly, and anyone can contribute under a license.

14
00:01:31.942 --> 00:01:35.372
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.368
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:41.418 --> 00:01:43.181
Community-driven!

17
00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:49.859
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.059
Contribute!

19
00:01:52.021 --> 00:02:00.697
Did you know? Many major technologies, like parts of the internet itself, rely on open source software built by volunteers worldwide!

20
00:02:00.747 --> 00:02:03.036
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:04.284 --> 00:02:15.431
Think and answer. What is one benefit of open source software being available for anyone to see and improve?

22
00:02:15.481 --> 00:02:16.631
Great answer!

23
00:02:17.743 --> 00:02:22.808
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
